<title>USA: Calif. Treasurer meets with bond firms in New York.</title>
<headline>Calif. Treasurer meets with bond firms in New York.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>California state Treasurer Matt Fong and the speaker of the state Assembly Curt Pringle met in New York on Wednesday with several bond firms to discuss the state's economy and political climate.</p>
<p>&quot;I felt it was important for the Speaker to meet with those whom we do business with, and to sell California's (economic) comeback story,&quot; Fong said.</p>
<p>Fong and Pringle began the meetings on Tuesday. The meetings were being held with several prominent Wall Street firms that underwrite bonds for the state of California.</p>
